 52	
 53	Start with \`data/keating.training.jsonl\`. It preserves source provenance, prompt context, model identity, explicit quality signals, deterministic split assignment, and character counts. Compatibility files are derived views.
 54	
 55	## Dataset summary
 56	
 57	- Generated: ${manifest.generatedAt ?? "unknown"}
 58	- Canonical records: ${counts.canonicalRecords ?? 0}
 59	- SFT-compatible examples: ${counts.examplesWritten ?? 0}
 60	- Train / validation: ${counts.trainRecords ?? 0} / ${counts.validationRecords ?? 0}
 61	- Exact duplicates removed: ${counts.duplicatesRemoved ?? 0}
 62	- Responses excluded from SFT: ${counts.sftExcluded ?? 0}
 63	- Redactions applied: ${counts.redactions ?? 0}
 64	
 65	## Quality labels
 66	
 67	- \`accepted\` (${quality.accepted ?? 0}): explicit helpful feedback or a learner-authored artifact; suitable for SFT review.
 68	- \`unscored\` (${quality.unscored ?? 0}): captured without a quality claim; review before training.
 69	- \`rejected\` (${quality.rejected ?? 0}): explicit missed feedback; excluded from positive SFT and retained for KTO/preference learning.
 70	- \`review\` (${quality.review ?? 0}) and \`reference\` (${quality.reference ?? 0}): retained for inspection, not recommended as positive SFT.
 71	
 72	## Files
 73	
 74	| Path | Records | Use |
 75	| --- | ---: | --- |
 76	${rows}
 77	
